commits.body:
P2-23's row is done, with its two commits. Four follow-ups are added
to the end of the table:
- the extern "C" definitions still to move to contract-named files
  (14.3);
- window.cpp's two driver exports, which are data and not functions;
- the mod interface's function pointers, which 13.4 does not cover as
  written;
- a stopped exception in a script link that is not charged to its mod.

Verified: the row and the rows added are in the tables' formats, and
nothing else on the page changed.

A row with a newer version gets its own Update button beside its menu;
with two or more updates the panel's head offers Update all, which
updates them one after another and says how many went through.
